. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 *
. 
.         * We construct an inequality index as dependent variable and name it 
> DV_H3. DV_H3 measures the deviation from an equal division of household labor
> , combining housework and childcare. First, we calculate the total number of 
> hours spent on these tasks by both partners. We then compute the male partner
> 's share of the total labor and define the inequality index as the absolute d
> eviation from an equal split: DV_H3 = abs(0.5 - male_share). 
.         *The independent variable is HasDaughter, a dummy variable coded as 1
>  if the respondent has least one daughter, 0 otherwise.
.         *We use a tobit regression since dependent variable is censored betwe
> en 0 and 0.5
.         *an additional note is that differently from the PAP we did not have 
> any religiousness measure in this data, hence we have omitted it from control
>  variables.
. 
.         tobit DV_H3 HasDaughter Age age_p YoungestAge both_employed pgisced11
> _clean pgisced11_p biokids, ll(0) ul(0.5)

